OL,3,AAfrica's richest man launches Kenya oil
OL,4,Arefinery despite land protests
OL,5,
OL,6,FNigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote and
OL,7,FKenya's President William Ruto have
OL,8,Fbroken ground on a $16bn (#12bn) oil
OL,9,Frefinery in Lamu, on Kenya's northern
OL,10,Fcoast.
OL,12,FUpon completion, the refinery is
OL,13,Fexpected to process 700,000 barrels of
OL,14,Fcrude oil a day, making it East
OL,15,FAfrica's largest industrial project by
OL,16,Fcapacity.
OL,18,FAhead of the launch, some local
OL,19,Fresidents took to the streets to demand
OL,20,Fmore compensation for land used for the
OL,21,Frefinery.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
